A||||2||Zman302||roof skin replacement||||1||
Z||000000||Zman302||07-20-2000||12:09 AM||||I'm getting ready to put my new sunroof skin on my car and was wondering what to use in place of the black tar that was under the skin holding it to the roof.  Can i use a ribbon seal like they used on windshields years ago or do i need to buy what was originally used at the factory.  Also i want to use something that won't get on the windshield since i will be leaving it in and may get it replaced down the road.  Any help on this will be greatly appreciated. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Zman302   <BR>84 sports coupe<BR>69 Z28 Camaro||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-20-2000||12:51 AM||||You can use the stuff from the original roof. If you don't have it I would suggest the tube of windsheild sealant. It won't dry superhard it dries to a more rubber type of consistancy. You just need a bead to hold the roof down. You don't need to get close to the windsheild and the tube type of stuff can be used to hold down the rubber trim that is around the windsheild when you put it back on. (needs to be removed to replace roof.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Coop88||07-20-2000||03:53 PM||||How about using some butyl from a glass shop? It never hardens(from what I've seen), and glass shops use it to install windsheilds. Don't get it on your hands, though. Very sticky stuff. Hope this helps.||||reg||1
